-- ==========================================
--[[
	Two games that live in the menu itself.

	The one thing that makes this harder than it looks is input. WASD is the
	character's, and a mini-game that reads it with UserInputService would let
	you mine a block and walk off a roof with the same keypress. So the arcade
	binds its keys through ContextActionService at a high priority and SINKS
	them: while a game is open the keys belong to it and the character does not
	see them at all. Unbound the moment the window closes.

	Everything else is deliberately cheap. Tiles are a fixed pool of buttons
	that get recoloured rather than rebuilt, the loop only exists while the
	window is open, and both games run on the same connection.
--]]
